							<p class="kicker">Local &amp; private</p>
							<h2>Your files stay on your network.</h2>
							<p class="lead">
								Transfers go straight between your Mac and the phone over Wi-Fi. No
								account, no cloud relay, no telemetry — and the whole thing is
								MIT-licensed open source.
							</p>
							<ul class="feature-list">
								<li>
									<strong>LAN-only transport</strong>
									<span>Nothing touches a server. If the Wi-Fi is off, nothing moves.</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<strong>No account, no tracking</strong>
									<span>Install and go. No sign-up, no analytics, no ads.</span>
								</li>
								<li>
									<strong>Open source</strong>
									<span>MIT licensed. Read the code, file issues, send patches.</span>
								</li>
							</ul>
